# PyroSync Backend & ETL Pipeline

The `backend` package provides the offline data processing, JSON exporter, schema validator, and synthetic dataset generator for the PyroSync client application.

## Installation
```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .
pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
```

## CLI Usage

### Generate Synthetic Test Dataset
```bash
python -m pyrosync.cli synth --out ../frontend/public/datasets
```
This generates deterministic synthetic data (`"synthetic": true`) with known edge cases:
- Empty AOI cells (cells with zero historical detections)
- A calendar month with historical reference median = 0
- Pre-VIIRS operating period (< 2012-01)
- Partial month (2012-01)
- Terra-only operating period (2000-11 to 2002-06)
- Harmonized block present
- Deliberately malformed dataset copy (`../frontend/public/datasets/malformed/`) for error screen testing.

### Validate Dataset Files & Budgets
```bash
python -m pyrosync.cli check --data ../frontend/public/datasets
```
Checks:
- All required JSON files conform to JSON Schemas in `pyrosync/schemas/`.
- Total core bundle is $\le 3\text{ MB}$ gzipped.
- Each annual hotspot shard is $\le 3\text{ MB}$ gzipped.
- Reports density of harmonized array.

### Export Real Parquet Data (Milestone 1)
```bash
python -m pyrosync.cli export \
  --grid /path/to/california_grid_10km.parquet \
  --modis-cm /path/to/modis_cell_month.parquet \
  --viirs-cm /path/to/viirs_cell_month.parquet \
  --modis-det /path/to/modis_clean.parquet \
  --viirs-det /path/to/viirs_clean.parquet \
  --boundary /path/to/california_boundary_2024.geojson \
  --out ../frontend/public/datasets
```

## Running Tests
```bash
pytest
ruff check pyrosync/ tests/
```

